{#
  Confirmation for a service-contributed deployment action (see DeploymentAction).

  Loaded into the shared modal shell by openServiceModal(), so a service's action asks
  the same way as everything else on this page instead of through window.confirm().
  The endpoint is filled in server-side from the action the service offered; this
  template never sees a URL from the request.

  Expects: action (DeploymentAction), message.

  The CSRF header lives on the wrapping div, NOT on the button: htmx inherits it from an
  ancestor, and a ROOS <c-button> re-emits attribute values in double quotes, which
  mangles the JSON of hx-headers.

  On confirm the endpoint answers with the shared progress fragment and htmx swaps it
  into this dialog, replacing the question with the running task. That is the whole
  reason these actions are tasks: sleeping a deployment commits to git and then runs the
  reprocessing pipeline, ArgoCD sync included, so there is real progress to follow rather
  than a request to wait out.
#}
<div data-deployment-action="true"
     hx-headers='{"X-CSRF-Token": "{{ request.state.csrf_token }}"}'
     hx-target="this"
     hx-swap="innerHTML">
    <div class="edit-section-content">
        <c-layout-flow gap="md">
            <c-p>{{ message }}</c-p>
            <div id="deployment-action-error" class="edit-section-error" style="display: none;"></div>
        </c-layout-flow>
    </div>
    <div class="edit-section-actions">
        <c-button type="button" label="Annuleren" kind="tertiary" @click="closeEditModal()" />
        <c-button
            type="button"
            label="{{ action.label }}"
            kind="{{ action.kind }}"
            showIcon="before"
            icon="{{ action.icon }}"
            hx-post="{{ action.endpoint }}"
            hx-disabled-elt="this" />
    </div>
</div>
